    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This thesis examines the role of Ben Okri's The Famished Road (1991) in the canon of African literature. The unique narrative structure of the novel opens up possibilities of interpretation beyond the potentially limiting scales of analysis often associated with the African novel, including tribe, nation, race, and continent.",
